1
00:04:57,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Where second best never gets a second chance.

2
00:09:54,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Crossroads is a drama, music, mystery film directed by Walter Hill.

3
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:57,000
A wanna-be blues guitar virtuoso seeks a long-lost song
by legendary musician, Robert Johnson.

4
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:54,000
Eugene Martone, played by Ralph Macchio.

5
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:51,000
Willie Brown, played by Joe Seneca.

6
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:48,000
Frances, played by Jami Gertz.

7
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:45,000
Scratch's Assistant, played by Joe Morton.

8
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:42,000
Scratch, played by Robert Judd.

9
00:44:33,000 --> 00:44:39,000
Jack Butler, played by Steve Vai.

10
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Crossroads is a 1986 American musical drama film, inspired by
the legend of blues musician Robert Johnson.

11
00:54:27,000 --> 00:54:33,000
It is directed by Walter Hill from a screenplay by John Fusco, and
stars Ralph Macchio, Joe Seneca and Jami Gertz.

12
00:59:24,000 --> 00:59:30,000
It features an original score by Ry Cooder featuring classical guitar
by William Kanengiser and harmonica by Sonny Terry.

13
01:04:21,000 --> 01:04:27,000
Steve Vai appears in the film as the devil's virtuosic
guitar player in the climactic guitar duel.

14
01:09:18,000 --> 01:09:24,000
Fusco was a traveling blues musician prior to attending New York University Tisch School of the Arts, where
he wrote Crossroads as an assignment in a master class led by Waldo Salt and Ring Lardner Jr.

15
01:14:15,000 --> 01:14:21,000
The student screenplay won first place in the national FOCUS Awards (Films of college and
University Students) and was sold to Columbia Pictures while Fusco was still a student.

16
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
The film was released by Columbia Pictures on March 14, 1986.

17
01:24:09,000 --> 01:24:15,000
Although Crossroads received positive reviews from
critics, it was not a financial success.

18
01:29:06,000 --> 01:29:12,000
However, it has been considered a cult classic,
particularly among musicians and guitarists.

19
01:34:03,000 --> 01:34:09,000
The tone is emotional and mind_bending.
